        "title": "More dead bodies than anticipated",
        "text": "We thought we'd be seeing some beautiful temples but the experience was more confronting than anticipated with at least 3 cremations occurring whilst we visited. The access to much of the temple complex is restricted for those who aren't Hindu and we didn't want to intrude upon families' grief by staring at the bodies of their loved ones. It seemed a bit macabre. The river where the cremations occur is very dirty and full of pigeons and monkeys. This was also the place we experienced the most begging and hawking in Kathmandu. Whilst an interesting cultural experience, it wasn't for me and I wouldn't go there again.",
